# One line-ending convention everywhere.
#
# The repository already stores LF in every blob, but a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the working tree, which produced a mixed
# tree (files written by tooling stayed LF, files written by git became CRLF).
# Prettier is configured for LF, so that mix makes `pnpm format:check` fail on
# files nobody edited. `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the object store on
# every platform. No blob changes, so this adds no commit churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data fixtures and docs are text and must stay diffable.
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
